add('2:e',['A3.2.6'],'A booking relation contains VisitorID,VisitorName,GuideID,GuideName,Specialism,VisitTime,RouteID,RouteName,Fee. VisitorID determines VisitorName; GuideID determines GuideName and Specialism; RouteID determines RouteName and Fee. Each booking has a unique BookingID and exactly one visitor, guide and route. Construct a 3NF schema, labelling primary and foreign keys.','VISITOR(VisitorID PK,VisitorName); GUIDE(GuideID PK,GuideName,Specialism); ROUTE(RouteID PK,RouteName,Fee); BOOKING(BookingID PK,VisitorID FK,GuideID FK,RouteID FK,VisitTime).',[(1,'VISITOR with correct key and attributes.'),(1,'GUIDE with correct key and attributes.'),(1,'ROUTE with correct key and attributes.'),(1,'BOOKING with key, VisitTime and references.'),(1,'Foreign keys identified; no transitive names/fees retained in BOOKING.')],[8],status='B',adapt='Supplies explicit functional dependencies and unique booking identifier, resolving source ambiguity about treatment cost and specialties.')
add('3:a',['A3.1.1'],'Outline how a foreign-key constraint can preserve integrity when a loan record refers to a museum member.','It requires the referenced member ID to exist in MEMBER, preventing a loan from referring to a nonexistent member.',[(1,'Requires an existing referenced member key.'),(1,'Explains prevention of orphan/misattributed loan data.')],[9],status='B',adapt='Narrows a broad old integrity-strategy question to relational integrity explicitly within A3.1.1.')
add('3:b',['A3.4.2'],'Outline what it means for a data warehouse to contain integrated data from several museum branches.','Data from the branches is combined into a unified representation, with compatible identifiers/formats, so analysis can compare records across branches.',[(1,'Combines multiple sources.'),(1,'Consistent representation supports cross-source analysis.')],[9],status='B',adapt='Reframes old integrated database terminology as the explicit integrated-data role of warehouses.')
