add('7:b-ii',['B2.3.2'],'Construct Python selection assigning label="inside" when d<1, and label="outside" otherwise.','if d < 1:\n    label = "inside"\nelse:\n    label = "outside"',[(1,'Both correct branches including boundary d=1.')],[22],status='B')
c='''def estimate(labels):
    count = 0
    for label in labels:
        if label == "inside":
            count += 1
    return 4 * count / len(labels)'''
add('7:c',['B2.2.2','B2.3.2','B2.3.3'],'A nonempty list labels contains "inside" or "outside". A supplied estimation rule is 4 times the number of "inside" entries divided by the total entries. Construct estimate(labels) in Python using a loop to return that value.','One solution:\n'+c,[(1,'Scans all labels.'),(1,'Counts only inside entries.'),(1,'Returns correct supplied ratio.')],[22],status='B',code=c,test_code=c+'\nassert estimate(["inside","outside","inside","inside"])==3\nassert estimate(["outside"])==0',check='Executed mixed and zero-inside cases.',adapt='Changes spreadsheet formula to Python traversal/selection with mathematical rule supplied, so no Monte Carlo theory is required.')
add('7:d',['A1.1.2','A1.1.4','A4.1.2'],'Evaluate the processing and memory needs of an ML camera system that detects many moving objects in a live image stream.','A GPU can process many similar image operations in parallel, improving throughput. RAM holds frames, model data and intermediate results; larger frames/more objects increase working data. Powerful hardware costs energy and money, while insufficient throughput increases delay and stale decisions. Choose enough GPU/RAM for measured frame-rate and latency requirements rather than assuming a simple box overlay means the whole detection task is cheap.',[(1,'GPU parallel processing benefit.'),(1,'Concrete live-image workload explanation.'),(1,'RAM working-data role.'),(1,'Develops capacity/latency/cost trade-off.'),(1,'Supported contextual hardware judgment.')],[23],status='B')
