add('8:e',['A4.3.8'],'Compare two ANN applications: recognizing a spoken command from audio features and proposing a missing word from a sentence. Refer to their inputs, outputs and one shared limitation. No detailed language-model architecture is required.','The speech system takes audio-derived features, whereas the missing-word system takes a representation of written context. Their outputs are a recognized command/category and a proposed word respectively. Both learn complex patterns from training data; biased or unrepresentative examples can produce incorrect predictions, so an output should not be treated as guaranteed understanding.',[(1,'Audio-feature input.'),(1,'Written-context input, explicitly compared.'),(1,'Recognized command/category output.'),(1,'Proposed-word output, explicitly compared.'),(1,'Shared learned-pattern/data limitation.'),(1,'Explains wrong prediction/need for checking.')],[25,26],status='B',adapt='Retains comparison of neural pattern-recognition applications; removes advanced NLP architecture, linguistic semantics and unsupported universal real-time/continuous-learning claims.')

